        "title": "chore: sync canonical autoreview skill",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw's bundled autoreview skill had drifted behind the canonical `openclaw/agent-skills` copy. It lacked custom Codex model defaults, fast-mode selection, newer reviewer engines, and later compatibility/isolation hardening.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nSynchronize `.agents/skills/autoreview` from the canonical shared skill, including `AUTOREVIEW_CODEX_MODEL`, `AUTOREVIEW_CODEX_SPEED`, repeatable Codex config overrides, deterministic tests, and preserved legacy Cursor aliases. The final source incorporates canonical PRs openclaw/agent-skills#48, #49, and #50. The two source trees match exactly.\n\nSecurity review also found repository-controlled configuration and MCP injection paths. The canonical implementation now isolates Codex, Pi, and Cursor review execution. Droid fails closed because its current CLI cannot guarantee a complete tool-free run.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMaintainers can set a private `AUTOREVIEW_CODEX_MODEL` value and `AUTOREVIEW_CODEX_SPEED=fast` in shell/launcher environment, or use an untracked repository-local environment loader such as `.envrc`. Autoreview does not create or own a defaults file.\n\nCodex accepts the custom model name. Fast mode is requested as its `priority` service tier and only applies when that model's catalog metadata advertises support.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- AI-assisted change; no transcript attached.\n- Canonical and bundled source trees compared identical, excluding generated Python bytecode.\n- Skill manifest validation and skill-creator validation passed.\n- Built-in autoreview self-tests passed.\n- Compatibility suite: 19 tests passed.\n- Hardening suite: 20 tests passed.\n- `cursor-agent` engine and binary compatibility aliases dry-run verified.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Final focused autoreview using a shell-provided custom model, high reasoning, and fast mode: clean, confidence 0.95.\n- Fresh `~/Projects/codex` pull at `be33f80bc65159c094ecd06bf155afa3061ce23d`; verified `codex-rs/protocol/src/config_types.rs:475`, `codex-rs/core/src/config/mod.rs:3558`, and `codex-rs/core/src/session/mod.rs:900`.\n",
